Research Question 3 (RQ3): Is there a connection between RBIs and player\'92s birth month? In other words, does the month the player was born in influence the total amount of RBIs in their career? To minimize data noise, only retired players will be analyzed for this question.\
Hypothesis 3 (H3): The team believes there is a weak correlation between RBIs and birth months for MLB players. There are multiple variables that affect a player\'92s ability to hit RBIs, including the birth location, or high school location elevation. Additionally, a player\'92s genetic makeup may influence oxygen saturation level (see, for example, Gibbens [2018] article on the Bajau\'92s people ability to stay underwater for up to 13 minutes without physical harm).\
